      "analysis": "Overview:\nThe analysis section focuses on identifying defects, anomalies, and discrepancies in the telemetry acquisition subsystem design as discussed during Design Review Meeting 04 (MoM_DesignReview04). This includes reviewing decisions made, action items assigned, requirement changes implemented, and test outcomes that highlight performance issues.\n\nDecisions Made:\n\nTime-tagged Sample Buffer Implementation: The decision was made to implement a time-tagged sample buffer for all channels in the acquisition subsystem (Decision: REQ-0005). This ensures accurate timestamping of data samples which is critical for telemetry analysis and synchronization across different systems.\n\nVersioning REST Interface: It was agreed that the REST interface should be versioned from day one to facilitate easier updates, maintenance, and compatibility with future software versions (Decision: REQ-0005).\n\nAction Items:\n\nClarify Sampling Rate in SysRS: An action item was assigned to Dr. Sharma to update Section 2 of System Requirements Specification (SysRS) to clarify the sampling rate requirement for REQ-0001, with a due date set for September 1, 2026.\n\nConfirm Authentication Mechanism: Lt. Rao is tasked with confirming the authentication mechanism specified in REQ-0008 with the security panel by September 15, 2026.\n\nRequirement Changes:\n\nStructured JSON Logging Output: REQ-0006 was modified to require structured JSON logging output for enhanced data processing and analysis capabilities.\n\nAdd Automatic Fault Recovery: A new requirement (REQ-0011) was added alongside existing REQ-0009, mandating automatic fault recovery within 30 seconds.\n\nTest Outcomes:\n\nPASS: Sampling Rate Compliance: REQ-0001 passed the test with all three channels acquired during the hardware-in-loop demonstration, indicating that the sampling rate requirements were met.\n\nFAIL: Latency Budget Violation: REQ-0005 failed due to the sample retrieval endpoint not meeting latency budget during load testing, highlighting a performance issue that needs addressing.\n\nPASS: MTBF Performance: REQ-0002 passed with an MTBF estimate recorded above 2000 hours on the reference platform, indicating robust operational reliability.\n\nThis analysis provides insights into the design's current state and areas requiring attention or improvement based on the outcomes of Design Review Meeting 04."
    },
